From 98bd3e4d4c39de960010345ef52bcd788286b6d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrissorr <cjs7477@g.rit.edu>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:18:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Correct PEM X509 docs regarding TRUSTED CERTIFICATE blocks

The documentation stated that the X509 PEM functions also process
trusted certificates, discarding the trust settings.  In fact, they
reject "TRUSTED CERTIFICATE" blocks;  only the X509_AUX functions
accept them.  Update the text accordingly.

Resolves: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/33019
CLA: trivial
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Merge-date: Sun Oct 11 21:31:53 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33166
(cherry picked from commit 22d309a11839d7c505af63c54880e657fc4bab5c)
---
 doc/man3/PEM_read_bio_PrivateKey.pod | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/man3/PEM_read_bio_PrivateKey.pod b/doc/man3/PEM_read_bio_PrivateKey.pod
index 22a5d606b0db..4a3d7ae74044 100644
--- a/doc/man3/PEM_read_bio_PrivateKey.pod
+++ b/doc/man3/PEM_read_bio_PrivateKey.pod
@@ -293,8 +293,9 @@ structure. The parameters are encoded using a PKCS#3 DHparameter
 structure.
 
 The B<X509> functions process an X509 certificate using an X509
-structure. They will also process a trusted X509 certificate but
-any trust settings are discarded.
+structure. They will not process a trusted X509 certificate (a PEM
+block of type "TRUSTED CERTIFICATE"); use the B<X509_AUX> functions
+to read those.
 
 The B<X509_ACERT> functions process an X509 attribute certificate using
 an X509_ACERT structure.
